---
// How lid-closed mode stays passwordless, in one paragraph.
import Chevron from './Chevron.astro';
---

<section id="how" class="approve wrap" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <h2 id="how-title" class="head" data-reveal>Approve it once</h2>
  <div class="body" data-reveal style="--i:1">
    <p>
      Keeping a Mac awake with the lid shut needs root. The first time you turn on Lid Closed <Chevron /> Keep Awake,
      Restless offers to set up a small helper whose only job is <code class="cmd">pmset disablesleep</code>. Approve
      “Restless” once in System Settings <Chevron /> General <Chevron /> Login Items &amp; Extensions, and it never
      asks for a password again.
    </p>
    <p class="aside">
      Rather not install anything? Choose Just This Time for a single password prompt instead. You can remove the
      helper whenever you like.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .approve {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: var(--gutter);
    padding-top: clamp(7rem, 14vw, 13rem);
  }

  h2 {
    grid-column: 1 / span 4;
  }

  .body {
    grid-column: 6 / span 7;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .body p {
    font-size: var(--step-lead);
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .body .aside {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--step-body);
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .approve {
      display: block;
    }

    .body {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
